1
00:05:28,421 --> 00:05:34,421
Spooks: The Greater Good is a thriller, action film directed by Bharat Nalluri.

2
00:10:56,842 --> 00:11:02,842
During a handover to the head of counter-terrorism of MI5,
Harry Pearce, a terrorist escapes custody.

3
00:16:25,263 --> 00:16:31,263
When Harry disappears soon after, his protégé is tasked with finding out what happened as an
impending attack on London looms, and eventually uncovers a deadly conspiracy.

4
00:21:53,684 --> 00:21:59,684
Harry Pearce, played by Peter Firth.

5
00:27:22,105 --> 00:27:28,105
Will Holloway, played by Kit Harington.

6
00:32:50,526 --> 00:32:56,526
Adem Qasim, played by Elyes Gabel.

7
00:38:18,947 --> 00:38:24,947
Geraldine Maltby, played by Jennifer Ehle.

8
00:43:47,368 --> 00:43:53,368
Oliver Mace, played by Tim McInnerny.

9
00:49:15,789 --> 00:49:21,789
June Keaton, played by Tuppence Middleton.

10
00:54:44,210 --> 00:54:50,210
Spooks: The Greater Good (known as MI-5 in some countries) is a 2015 British spy film,
continuing from the 2002–2011 British television spy series Spooks.

11
01:00:12,631 --> 01:00:18,631
Jonathan Brackley and Sam Vincent wrote the
script, with Bharat Nalluri directing.

12
01:05:41,052 --> 01:05:47,052
Peter Firth reprises his role as Harry Pearce, who
appeared in all ten series of the programme.

13
01:11:09,473 --> 01:11:15,473
Also returning from the TV series are Tim McInnerny as Oliver Mace, Lara Pulver as Erin
Watts, Hugh Simon as Malcolm Wynn-Jones, and Geoffrey Streatfeild as Calum Reed.

14
01:16:37,894 --> 01:16:43,894
Kit Harington and Jennifer Ehle star as new characters in leading roles.

15
01:22:06,315 --> 01:22:12,315
The film was released on 8 May 2015.

16
01:27:34,736 --> 01:27:40,736
Upon its release, it received generally mixed reviews from critics.

17
01:33:03,157 --> 01:33:09,157
The film explores themes of corruption, escape, police, explosive, kidnapping.

18
01:38:31,578 --> 01:38:37,578
The tone is intense.
